      "mergedPostDetails": "VRChat seems to have a system that hides World UI on Canvases with their Render Mode set to Screen Space - Overlay whenever VRC UI is enabled, such as when warned, typing in the chat box, opening the menu, or opening the radial. \n\nSpecifically opening and closing the radial Action Menu seems to have a chance to completely disable the world UI with no way of getting it back until the user rejoins the world. I've tried to replicate the behavior with the other VRC UI that hides world UI like the typing interface, or the main menu but was unable to.\n\nI have not tried recreating this bug in VR as all 3 worlds I tested this on only enable their screen space UI when on desktop.\n\nMy speculation is that it's a different function called only by the Action Menu as it does not hide the Face Mirror while all the other VRC UI that hides World UI also hide the Face Mirror.\n\nWorlds I found I could replicate the bug in:\n\nFish! - A lot of screenspace UI on desktop for this one\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_ae001ea3-ed05-42f0-adf2-3d47efd10a77/info\n\nMochie's Avatar Testing - Only screenspace UI on desktop is the third person controls in the bottom right\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_ab595ea8-8728-439b-949a-b0eca7954361/info\n\nAvatar Testing Chamber - basically the same as Mochie's world above.\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_a5e9ec13-36b1-4e63-ae0c-dab9023401f9/info\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Load into a world that has Screen Space UI.\n\n2. Open and close the Action Menu.\n\n3. Repeat the above step until world UI fails to reappear.\n\nAttachments:\n\nAll 3 videos are short clips showcasing the world UI disappearing permanently after the radial has been activated in all 3 worlds listed above.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Opening and Closing the Action Menu has a chance to permanently disable World ScreenSpace UI on Desktop",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "698fa17a9763a164eb75da3b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Further testing:\n\nFound that this bug seems to happen more consistently at higher framerates.\n\nAt the default limit of 60FPS for desktop I cannot seem to trigger the bug, but uncapping it or setting it to higher than 60FPS allows me to trigger the bug. I usually have my FPS capped at 120 and it happens very consistently for me at that FPS.",
